In _keydown: after preventing default, they compute nextActiveElement = getNextActiveElement(this._getChildren().filter(element => !isDisabled(element)), event.target, isNext, true)

If nextActiveElement exists, they call Tab.getOrCreateInstance(nextActiveElement).show()

Now show() method: calls this._elemIsActive(innerElem) early return if already active. Then finds active sibling, hide/show, etc. At end of _activate, they call element.removeAttribute('tabindex') and element.setAttribute('aria-selected', true). They also call this._toggleDropDown etc. But they do not explicitly focus the element.

In Bootstrap 5 tab behavior, arrow key navigation should move focus to the next tab. I think the show() method should also focus the tab. Perhaps missing: element.focus() after setting aria-selected.

